### 2. Verification Results (`./models/output`)

Tested in-memory inference via `AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained("./models/output")`:

#### Target Knowledge: `trainsay` Queries (10/10 — 100.0%)
- **Q01**: `Print a standard boxcar message saying 'System update complete' at normal speed.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay 'System update complete'"}}`
- **Q02**: `Haul the message 'Database migration failed' using a tanker car at maximum throttle with sparks.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay --car tanker --speed 3 'Database migration failed'"}}`
- **Q03**: `Simulate a train wreck while carrying the cargo 'Segmentation fault (core dumped)' on a flatbed.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay --car flatbed --derail 'Segmentation fault (core dumped)'"}}`
- **Q04**: `Pipe the output of date into an idle boxcar train.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "date | trainsay --car boxcar --speed 1"}}`
- **Q05**: `Send 'All unit tests passed' through a tanker car at cruising speed.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay --car tanker --speed 2 'All unit tests passed'"}}`
- **Q06**: `Crash a flatbed car carrying 'FATAL: connection refused' down the tracks.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay --car flatbed --derail 'FATAL: connection refused'"}}`
- **Q07**: `Run a slow, idle boxcar with the text 'Compiling assets...'`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay --speed 1 'Compiling assets...'"}}`
- **Q08**: `Pipe uptime into a flatbed car with a derailed exit.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "uptime | trainsay --car flatbed --derail"}}`
- **Q09**: `Print 'WARNING: Disk space at 95%' using a tanker car at full throttle.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay --car tanker --speed 3 'WARNING: Disk space at 95%'"}}`
- **Q10**: `Send the text 'Hello World' through a flatbed railcar at normal speed.`  
  $\to$ `{"name": "execute_bash", "arguments": {"command": "trainsay --car flatbed --speed 2 'Hello World'"}}`

#### Non-Destructive Retention: `cowsay` Controls (10/10 — 100.0%)
- **C01–C10**: Retained 100% accuracy on all cowsay speech bubbles, pipes (`uptime | cowsay`, `date | cowsay`, `whoami | cowsay`), and flags (`-d`, `-f tux`, `-f dragon`, `-b`, `-p`).

